<newsitem itemid="47328" id="root" date="1996-09-11" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Antofagasta half year profit 27 mln stg.</title>
<headline>Antofagasta half year profit 27 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		11.9		   vs 24.2</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 2.0		    vs 2.0</p>
<p> Pretax		     27.0		   vs 51.6</p>
<p> Turnover		   95.2		   vs 87.8</p>
<p>NOTE - Mining to transport group Antofagasta Holdings Plc said profits in the first half last year included exceptional gains of 15.8 million stg.  </p>
<p> Operating result	 19.1		   vs 29.2</p>
<p> Exceptional		nil		    vs 15.8</p>
<p> Interest  paid	   0.6		    vs 1.4 received</p>
<p> Tax			  3.8		    vs 6.0</p>
<p> Net taxed		  23.2		   vs 45.6</p>
<p> Pay date		   December 6</p>
<p>Div registration date  November 5</p>
<p> Ex-div date		October 28</p>
<p>NOTE - Antofagasta, which has copper mining interests, said the outlook for copper continued to be uncertain and a recovery to higher prices in the future was unlikely.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
